From: matthane <matthan.evans@icloud.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 09:46:19 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayer: close a parked video stream without draining it
 again

A playlist join closed the parked video stream and waited for its
queue to drain, although parking had already waited for the stream's
end. A decoder that never reported its last picture timed out a
second time there and froze the held picture for another 5 s.
---
 xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp
@@ -0,7 +0,8 @@
       if (m_joinPending && m_CurrentVideo.id >= 0)
       {
         aml_continue_presentation(hint);
-        CloseStream(m_CurrentVideo, true);
+        // parking waited for the stream's end, so nothing is left to drain
+        CloseStream(m_CurrentVideo, false);
         m_joinPending = false;
       }
       res = OpenVideoStream(hint, reset);
